  "term": "ascending reticular activating system",
  "definition": "The ascending reticular activating system is a central nervous system system involved in arousing the cortical and limbic parts of the brain. In the packet, reducing activity through GABA-A receptors in this system is described as blocking arousal and producing sedative and hypnotic effects.",
